00:45:35.780 --> 00:45:38.230
This is a great point in a sense that

00:45:40.870 --> 00:45:43.400
unlike in a blackbox optimization,

00:45:43.400 --> 00:45:46.440
where we're going to fix, or decide,

00:45:46.440 --> 00:45:49.900
choose one particular
hyper-parameters configuration

00:45:49.900 --> 00:45:52.090
and train them all the way to the end,

00:45:52.090 --> 00:45:54.580
and then evaluate the validation loss.

00:45:54.580 --> 00:45:57.260
We are going to actually
update the hyper-parameters

00:45:57.260 --> 00:45:58.093
on the fly.

00:45:58.093 --> 00:46:00.610
What that means is that
the may actually change

00:46:00.610 --> 00:46:02.720
as the training continues.

00:46:02.720 --> 00:46:06.410
All of course is a big question,
whether this is necessary

00:46:06.410 --> 00:46:09.220
